(Bug #55's other half: when the collection's element type cannot be
 proven - here a list widened by a later append - the analyzer has
 nothing to reject, so codegen must not read the match value as text to
 compare it. A number can never equal text, so the substitution simply
 never fires and every element comes through unchanged.)

a list called words is ["a"].
append "b" to words.
print each item from words treating 98 as 31.
